.TH "WORKERNAVIGATOR.PLATFORM" "3JS" "April 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
WorkerNavigator.platform \- WorkerNavigator: platform property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is only available in Web Workers.
.PP
Returns a string representing the platform of the browser.
The specification allows browsers to always return the empty string, so
don\(cqt rely on this property to get a reliable answer.
.SH VALUE
A string identifying the platform on which the browser is running, or an
empty string if the browser declines to (or is unable to) identify the
platform.
\f[CR]platform\f[R] is a string that must be an empty string or a string
representing the platform on which the browser is executing.
.PP
For example: \f[CR]\(dqMacIntel\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dqWin32\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqFreeBSD i386\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dqWebTV OS\(dq\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
console.log(navigator.platform);
.EE
.SH USAGE NOTES
On Windows, modern browsers return \f[CR]\(dqWin32\(dq\f[R] even if
running on a 64\-bit version of Windows
